    "lightning_ready": true,
    "bitcoin_integration": "Malta is the EU's most crypto-forward jurisdiction, self-branded the 'Blockchain Island' since 2018. The MFSA has regulated crypto assets since 2018 under the Virtual Financial Assets Act (Chapter 590) via the VFA framework (categories determined by the Financial Instrument Test), supplemented by the MTAS/MDIA and ITAS legislation. Since 2024-2026 the EU Markets in Crypto-Assets Regulation (MiCA) is the primary framework (Markets in Crypto-Assets Act, Ch. 647); the VFA regime is transitional and phasing out as crypto-asset service providers (CASPs) migrate to MiCA (roughly by mid-2026). Official stance is pro-innovation and welcoming; Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies qualify as Virtual Financial Assets and are licencable. BTC is not legal tender (euro is the currency)."
